  "scientific_summary": "r530 zero qualified survivors, first Claude Opus 5.5 round. 352895: an author-complete proof that for odd p and coprime positive A,B some n has p not dividing phi(An+B), by Dirichlet with a prime or, when p|A and B=1 mod p, a product of two primes. Root hand-checked the three cases and they hold. Root adopts the author recommendation EXCLUDE AS ROUTINE, credit 0, as a source-ingredient extension: source Proposition 3.5 already picks a prime by Dirichlet, and the two-prime variant closes the single remaining case, the same pattern as prior source-ingredient exclusions. Strongest dissent recorded: it is a deliberate printed conjecture, the authors wrote that their methods cannot address it, and no earlier proof was found in one bounded search. The user may overrule. 372582: routine Weil reduction, expensive Lean, zero. 381174: direct application of Komlos-Pintz-Szemeredi, zero, very expensive Lean. 352894 and 318354 are proved in their own sources, zero. 370850 and 320444 partial. Twelve others parked after the literal only. Disclosed deviations: the get_g8 runner receipt shows exit 0 although the guard exited 1 because of a wrapper sys.exit(0), and one direct ls of the lane plans directory ran outside the runner. This lane hashed corpus lines without their trailing newline; root re-derived all twenty against the corpus in that form. Verified 185 manifest files, 20 corpus bindings, 13 frozen, 10 charged GET hops (7 PDF, 3 redirects, 1 rejected cookie cycle), 3 searches / 3 strings with responses saved. Credit 0, 57/80.",
  "root_disposition": "ZERO_QUALIFIED_SURVIVORS_352895_EXCLUDED_ROUTINE_ROOT_HAND_CHECKED_USER_MAY_OVERRULE",
